landing-review: landing 10 (the duplicate engine-frame upload), level medium, 2026-09-18

Range main...HEAD at dcbe2bb..0089d17, main at 5896b1f; a dedicated read-only
reviewer with the pristine build and objdump. NO HIGH findings. Three MEDIUM,
five LOW, four NIT. All twelve verified against the code before acting.

M1 -- "the second bound on the engine frame's dimensions went with it" wrong in
the commit message and in two notes. SURF_MAXDIM 8192 still stands at
tagpu_vk_gui.c:1675 and is still downstream of TAGPU_SURF_MAXDIM 4096, so it
still bounds nothing. What went is what it protected: the mk_image and the
memcpy sized by it. Corrected in gpu-status.md and roadmap.md.

M2 -- the plan's own correction to item 10 ended in two sentences the landing
disproved (that landing 10 would delete the layer semantics, and that the
786 432 bytes a frame are not waste), and the paragraph I had written above it
endorsed the whole correction wholesale. Verified against what landed: neither
uSurf nor the layer semantics went, and the SECOND copy WAS waste. The two
sentences are struck in place as a quotation with the correction under them,
and the endorsement is narrowed to the part that still holds.

M3 -- A REAL REGRESSION THIS LANDING INTRODUCED, and the most valuable finding
of the twelve. Borrowing tagpu_vk_surf.c's image coupled the whole UI composite
to that pass's ST_REFUSED latch (set :584 on a slot allocation failure,
deliberately preserved by tagpu_vk_surf_down at :796, therefore permanent for
the process). One failed vkCreateImage under VRAM pressure would have taken the
panels, the minimap and the cursor for the session, where before the landing
only the bottom layer stopped. Verified by reading both paths. My own survey had
considered the build-time R8_UNORM refusal and NOT the runtime allocation path.
Fixed with a three-way check: no engine frame (refuse, as before) / a frame the
surface pass cannot lend (composite with the guard and the strict harness
disarmed, said once) / a frame it can (borrow).

LOW 4 -- the re-checked dimension bound in tagpu_vk_surf_prepare returned
without clearing haveSerial, leaving a stale slot addressable through the new
borrow and contradicting the header's own validity statement. It invalidates now.

LOW 5 -- folded into M3's test: LAY_FS clamps its fetch to the twin's size and
then texelFetches an image sized by the primary, so a primary smaller than the
twin read out of range. Predates this landing; bounded by it now.

LOW 6 -- "on every frame the surface changes" wrong: the upload ran on EVERY
frame. LOW 7 -- the live hazard note at :5458 named the now-dead s_engImg, and
the hazard is bounded by M3's new test. LOW 8 -- reframed from "a duplicate
upload nobody had noticed" to finishing the ownership move the plan's own 4c
section described and left half-done.

NIT 9 (header block above the teardown comment), 10 (the passes do not share a
sampler, and texelFetch ignores samplers anyway), 11 (cite :399/:407, not :398),
12 (uGuard on this lane comes from the hand-over at tagpu_gui_surf.c:2670 via
have_engine_frame at :807-810; the cited :2606 is the GL lane's uniform and is
dead here -- the conclusion survived, the cite did not).

Two rendering defects the wiki showed afterwards, neither of them findings of
the review: plan items 10 and 11 indent continuations four spaces where 1-9 use
three, which is python-markdown's code threshold, so 118 lines were shipping as
literal source; and `~~` renders as tildes because the builder loads no
strikethrough extension. Both fixed here. 80 other `~~` occurrences across 17
notes are still rendering as tildes -- corpus-wide, pre-existing, not this
landing's to fix.

Re-verified after the fixes by running it: a build A/B over the shell, three
captures each, cross-build 180-188 differing pixels against 182-186 within main
and 183-187 within this branch. noeng=0, skipped=0, overflows=0, fps=60.0, the
in-game frame stable to 0 px, zero "no image to lend" lines.

Findings acted on in e99ff63.
